{
  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250). All four scvi_n200+ViT multiprofile aggregation/fusion combinations are now tested, confirming transformer+weighted as optimal for that RNA encoder. The one remaining uncertainty at the top of the performance range is whether the RNA encoder choice still matters when paired with the strongest image encoder (ViT-L). config_027 isolates exactly this: it is identical to config_039 except PCA_n2000 replaces scvi_n200. In RNA-only settings, scvi_n200 beat PCA by ~0.035 (single) and likely more (multiprofile), but in a multimodal regime where the ViT provides a strong learned representation, a 2000-dim linear PCA might capture complementary variance that the 200-dim scvi bottleneck discards. This is the cleanest remaining A/B comparison, requires changing only one factor, and directly tests whether the best configuration found so far is truly optimal or whether a different RNA representation could push accuracy higher. As the final experiment, it either confirms config_039 as the winner or reveals a surprise, maximizing information under zero remaining budget."
}

